    text: "Runner qualification observation: a complete coverage run with concurrent whole-repository ESLint/typecheck timed out context-intent-calibration-gate.spec.ts real top-level entrypoint at120seconds. The identical focused file passes all11 cases in15.5seconds without that competing load. This is an environment/load observation, not a confirmed product-latency regression or a threshold waiver. The next full run will keep heavy independent checks sequential. Existing budgets and timeout remain unchanged; this owner remains open/unclaimed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-26T17:52:09.165Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "PR1596 local Node 26.12.1 measurements retained with unchanged policies: the complete static run passed functional checks but failed SDK import budgets on a qualified runner; an isolated run then missed only graph at 189/172 ms. A controlled immutable 61441f45a baseline and current candidate both subsequently pass all ten imports, and the normal current import gate passes. The CLI transport gate still fails locally. In a controlled exact main 46fd91415 versus candidate comparison, main fails next 450/440, create 404/398 and claim 424/415 ms (qualified control 74 ms); candidate fails get 374/362, create 407/398 and claim 416/415 ms (qualified control 53 ms). Both use unchanged ten-sample gates and isolated one-item trackers. These changing measurements do not establish patch causality or waive product admission; exact-head hosted static remains mandatory. No budget or runner-qualification rule is changed."
