    text: "Controlled follow-up preserves failed samples: the first isolated baseline was on tmpfs and therefore not a fair filesystem comparison. A fresh sibling Btrfs checkout of a20864701 passes original budgets (next410ms/create389ms/claim391ms). Applying only the three array-policy runtime changes and rebuilding in that same path yields qualified failures (next512ms/create462ms/claim487ms), while get improves339ms to311ms. Current original checkout also has qualified next473ms/create407ms failures. No threshold, qualification rule or outcome is changed. Phase-varying timing and read-only next must be distinguished from mutation-code cost; require the final hosted static/floor gate, and retain this evidence without asserting an established root cause."
